<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese bond report.</title>
<headline>Portuguese bond report.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bonds were treading water, waiting from some external impetus to galvanise trade which could come with the release of U.S. producer price data at 1230 GMT, traders said.</p>
<p>The market is not discounting any move in Bank of Portugal interest rates on Friday when it announces conditions for the next commercial bank reserve period. The announcement should come around 1315 GMT.</p>
<p>&quot;The market is gaining slightly along with Spain but most of Europe is quiet and lacking volatility,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>--Sergio Goncalves, Lisbon bureau 3511-3113122</p>
</text>
